# Manual review diff / change manifest
#
# This workspace is not a Git checkout.  The following is a concise semantic
# diff against D:/code/FPGA/runs/ultra-top-tcm, not a machine-applicable patch.
# Generated Verilator objects, CoreMark .map/.dis files, signatures, DCPs and
# Vivado reports are intentionally omitted from the source change list.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_branch_predict.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_branch_predict.v
@@ new module @@
+ Added parameterized, generate-disabled direct-mapped predictor.
+ Default CPU integration: SUPPORT_BRANCH_PREDICTION=0,
+ BRANCH_PREDICTOR_INDEX_W=6; enabled table has 64 entries and 24-bit tag.
+ Lookup index = lookup_pc_i[INDEX_W+1:2].
+ Tag = lookup_pc_i[31:INDEX_W+2], with valid && full-tag comparison.
+ Conditional branch direction uses BHT[1]; JAL uses is_jal => taken.
+ Target/tag/BHT/is_jal fields use explicit RAM64X1D instances for
+ asynchronous lookup and synchronous update; valid bits are resettable FF.
+ Reset/FENCE.I clear valid only. Replacement reseeds BHT from the resolved
+ outcome; hit updates saturate at 00/11. No update-to-lookup bypass.
+ JALR/RET are excluded by the execute-side update-valid contract.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_fetch.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_fetch.v
@@ ports and fetch metadata @@
+ Added prediction_taken_i/prediction_target_i inputs and prediction_pc_o /
+ fetch_pred_taken_o outputs.
+ Predictor target is selected only at the registered fetch-PC next-PC mux;
+ redirect request retains priority and sequential PC+4 remains the default.
+ Captured pred_taken is paired with pc_d_q on accepted instruction requests.
+ Skid buffer widened from 66 to 67 bits to carry pred_taken atomically with
+ faults, PC and instruction. Existing accept/stall/response-drop behavior is
+ retained.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_decode.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_decode.v
@@ decode payload @@
+ Added one prediction metadata bit to the decode interface and optional
+ extra-decode buffer. EXTRA_DECODE_STAGE=1 captures it with valid/fault/PC/
+ instruction; EXTRA_DECODE_STAGE=0 passes it through.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_issue.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_issue.v
@@ execute and redirect interface @@
+ Added fetch_pred_taken_i and opcode_pred_taken_o.
+ Added branch_d_exec_taken_i, branch_d_exec_mispredict_i and
+ branch_d_exec_correction_pc_i inputs.
+ branch_request_o = branch_csr_request_i | branch_d_exec_mispredict_i;
+ CSR/trap redirect remains the priority source for branch_pc_o/priv.
+ The existing issue/pipe-control branch-taken and branch-target meanings are
+ preserved; correctly predicted direct branches do not request a squash.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_exec.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_exec.v
@@ branch result split and update record @@
+ Added opcode_pred_taken_i.
+ Split actual-taken/target from front-end mispredict/correction outputs.
+ Correction is actual target for predicted-NT/actual-T and PC+4 for
+ predicted-T/actual-NT; direct JAL misses only when not predicted.
+ JALR/RET always retain the existing execution redirect and do not train the
+ first-version predictor.
+ Added a registered valid resolved update record carrying PC, target, JAL,
+ taken, prediction and mispredict information. Invalid, interrupted and
+ taken-misaligned direct instructions are excluded from update.
+ Added registered resolved-category observation signals for simulation stats.

--- baseline/core/riscv/riscv_core.v
+++ isolated/core/riscv/riscv_core.v
@@ parameters and wiring @@
+ Added SUPPORT_BRANCH_PREDICTION=0 and BRANCH_PREDICTOR_INDEX_W=6 parameters.
+ Added u_branch_predict between fetch-PC lookup and execute update record.
+ Connected FENCE.I valid invalidation, predictor lookup and update ports.
+ Connected prediction metadata through fetch/decode/issue/execute and the
+ split mispredict redirect interface.
+ Added ULTRA_PERF_COUNTERS simulation observers and Verilator-public readers;
+ these are not present in normal Vivado synthesis.

--- baseline/top_tcm_axi/src_v/riscv_tcm_top.v
+++ isolated/top_tcm_axi/src_v/riscv_tcm_top.v
@@ top-level parameters @@
+ Added and forwarded SUPPORT_BRANCH_PREDICTION=0 and
+ BRANCH_PREDICTOR_INDEX_W=6 to riscv_core.

